{"title":"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Logarithms)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Logarithms)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Beginner)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Beginner)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~1:10)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:10)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Ted mistakenly wrote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/4/4446ef7efda16c084ba5c976ee7729f373183908.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^m\\cdot\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4096}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"95\" height=\"45\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/9/5d95b42d9b2ee3a538690f497e19b91b93ed49ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot\\sqrt[m]{\\frac{1}{4096}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"92\" height=\"45\" /> What is the sum of all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> for which these two expressions have the same value?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/4/e14fed811bdf395ed28763cbb895f1db8be2968c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 5 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 6 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 7 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 8 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"353\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/c/69c2cbd459c37ee97c02bdebda6d4ce6f683286d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^m\\cdot\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4096}} = 2\\cdot\\sqrt[m]{\\frac{1}{4096}}.\\]\" width=\"205\" height=\"43\" />\nConverting everything into powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and equating exponents, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/9/7598fbe6ca643fe6ca275252661db555dd392544.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 2^m\\cdot(2^{-12})^{\\frac12} &amp;= 2\\cdot (2^{-12})^{\\frac1m} \\\\ 2^{m-6} &amp;= 2^{1-\\frac{12}{m}} \\\\ m-6 &amp;= 1-\\frac{12}{m}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"199\" height=\"96\" />\nWe multiply both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/d/1ed17364b06ad42c2450df4d0f6a0f06034086bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"13\" /> then rearrange as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/7/ba7288683f6d7ca5d6bd5e4ca6374dcd51a462c3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[m^2-7m+12=0.\\]\" width=\"147\" height=\"17\" />\nBy Vieta's Formulas, the sum of such values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/9/0892d2010fb1ad517d3c3509c62b65a0b9e08791.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 7}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"62\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/4/904f27995d33e0d39f43ec959e7cb100516e9396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/0/500fb9788ed8553a319dd49cb6262faebcacc88b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" /> from the quadratic equation above.\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM ~KingRavi\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Logarithms.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Logarithms)\">Solution 2 (Logarithms)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Logarithms)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can rewrite the equation using fractional exponents and take logarithms of both sides: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8ad34f0fe1b47ed121214e7b1e95c1bbccf49987.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_2{(2^{m}\\cdot4096^{-1/2}}) = \\log_2{(2\\cdot4096^{-1/m})}.\\]\" width=\"321\" height=\"21\" /> \nWe can then use the additive properties of logarithms to split them up: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/f/33f1cb31ada82645dd26181ea93e3e74aeb1c366.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_2{(2^{m})} + \\log_2{(4096^{-1/2})} = \\log_2{2} + \\log_2{(4096^{-1/m})}.\\]\" width=\"421\" height=\"21\" /> \nUsing the power rule, the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/5/3d5aa25baff7e61270e7c515649635da6684099d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4096 = 2^{12},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"20\" /> and bringing the exponents down, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/8/fb83ea4bcd188c2b98369f2778081d916cb47698.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} m - 6 &amp;= 1 - \\frac{12}{m} \\\\ m + \\frac{12}{m} &amp;= 7 \\\\ m^{2} + 12 &amp;= 7m \\\\ m^{2} - 7m + 12 &amp;= 0 \\\\ (m-3)(m-4) &amp;= 0, \\end{align*}\" width=\"197\" height=\"159\" />\nfrom which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/b/27b00129906b721ebe808a705e83d5df749a4ba3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 3$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/9/b6979b4da672f436799b1cc7f64c918c60612a94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" />. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/f/aff31fac00ce06992f75fc5d99b6f037bb5a6e68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+4 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 7}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"127\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>- youtube.com/indianmathguy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since third roots are conventionally positive integers, assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> can only be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f21c6bf272168826f18fdac932fe88dfe83450.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4096}}=\\frac{1}{64}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"106\" height=\"45\" />. Testing out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, we see that only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> work. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/a/deac5929cb9928ade8a6ede825419b202ff2e104.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+4=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"122\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~MrThinker\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Beginner.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Beginner)\">Solution 4 (Beginner)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Beginner)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/3/d931dde7123e9b09c298b3bcf6fa8c9d320aa225.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^m \\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4096}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"95\" height=\"45\" /> becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/2/552f62824059264488be8d02059fb67d1f25f7d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2^m}{64}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"28\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/6/3563567964e61c19e0f9b5ee39566123fd818436.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot \\sqrt[m]{\\frac{1}{4096}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"87\" height=\"45\" /> becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/c/a4ca1403971575f1d0750662292ac926160e3935.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2^{12}}})^{\\frac{1}{m}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"80\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/6/b26d0edea3b1d2f4219916418b19450ca1b64c82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{2^{\\frac{12}{m}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"31\" height=\"40\" />. Setting these two values equal and cross multiplying results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/6/ed6a3c5a6498087fd2b8a07b6e318baffef442b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$128=2^m \\cdot 2^{\\frac{12}{m}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"113\" height=\"19\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/4/4d486afd286d4b0869ab9f0c013efaffffb9609e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$128=2^{m+\\frac{12}{m}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"101\" height=\"19\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/c/cbcee6c324345c9c3cc167a40f099d0bd5ac95f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$128=2^7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"17\" />, and since all the numbers have the same base, the exponents become the new equation, resulting in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/3/e8319466ed744d3a2b0dd583a95252bb647ab823.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7=m+\\frac{12}{m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"96\" height=\"38\" />. Testing values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> results in two solutions: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/4/904f27995d33e0d39f43ec959e7cb100516e9396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/0/500fb9788ed8553a319dd49cb6262faebcacc88b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/2/0720aa8f7e4c3eefe3960ad92282609edafb5a6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+4=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/c/85ccbb6ee410251b01630d6d8f04a1ff41e96a9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }7}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"62\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>(note: this is my first time posting a solution, so things may not be formatted correctly. if the writing or LaTeX needs to be fixed, please fix it, thanks :D)\n</p><p>~epicfloppa\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_.28Logical.2C_Good_Editing.2C_.7E1:10.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~1:10)\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:10)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:10)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/okVcTrC3wwA\">https://www.youtube.com/shorts/okVcTrC3wwA</a>\n</p><p>~Ebai\n</p><p>Note: the problem where this is linked is the second problem covered (1:00-2:10)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1\">Video Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/UmaCmhwbZMU\">https://youtu.be/UmaCmhwbZMU</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/x716XmDDY9w\">https://youtu.be/x716XmDDY9w</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/0kkc4-y8TkU\">https://youtu.be/0kkc4-y8TkU</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>